#   - RAM Mode: Mounts a high-speed ext4 loopback image in memory.
#   - SSD Mode: Symlinks DATA_DIR to a persistent folder on your SSD.
#   The 'setup-seeder-cache.sh' script handles this logic based on RAM_CACHE_ENABLED.
# These settings define the "Backing Services" that the Go microservices depend on.
# Used by: Rest-API, Vault, Abuse-Store, URL-Store, Claims-Provider.
# The init-db.sql script creates separate databases (octor, vault, abuse_store, etc.) on first boot.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

